---
import type { ToolDefinition } from '../../types';
import { CATEGORIES } from '../../data/tools';

interface Props {
  tool: ToolDefinition;
}

const { tool } = Astro.props;
const categoryInfo = CATEGORIES.find((c) => c.id === tool.category);
const categoryName = categoryInfo?.name || 'Digital Utilities';
---

<div class="space-y-16 pt-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
  <!-- Section 1: Deep Dive Overview & Technical Architecture -->
  <section class="space-y-6">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-950/70 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 border border-purple-200 dark:border-purple-800">
      📚 Comprehensive Technical Manual & Reference
    </div>
    
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
      The Complete Guide to {tool.name}: Architecture, Best Practices & In-Browser Mastery
    </h2>

    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
      In today's fast-paced digital ecosystem, the demand for fast, reliable, and privacy-respecting utilities has never been greater. <strong>{tool.name}</strong> on Toolchemy represents a modern paradigm shift in web application engineering. Rather than relying on legacy server-side architectures that require uploading gigabytes of sensitive personal, business, or intellectual property files over the public internet, {tool.name} executes 100% client-side directly within the sandbox of your modern web browser.
    </p>

    <p class="text-base leading-relaxed">
      By leveraging high-performance browser APIs—such as HTML5 Canvas 2D and WebGL rendering contexts, WebAssembly (WASM) compiled binaries, Web Workers multi-threaded parallel computation, the Web Cryptography API (<code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">crypto.subtle</code>), and typed array buffers (<code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">Uint8Array</code>, <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">ArrayBuffer</code>)—{tool.name} harnesses the raw compute capabilities of your local CPU and GPU. The result is zero upload wait times, zero network bandwidth consumption, instantaneous real-time visual feedback, and cryptographic-grade privacy guarantees.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 pt-4">
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-3 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>⚡ Zero Latency Local Execution</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Traditional web converters queue your requests on overloaded cloud instances. Toolchemy bypasses all server roundtrips. Your files are ingested into browser RAM, processed instantaneously via local hardware threads, and downloaded directly to your disk with zero network bottlenecks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-3 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🛡️ Absolute Confidentiality & Compliance</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          For professionals governed by strict confidentiality mandates (such as GDPR, HIPAA, SOC 2, and NDAs), uploading documents to third-party cloud servers poses legal liabilities. With Toolchemy, bytes never leave your device, ensuring full regulatory compliance automatically.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Technical Specifications & Format Compatibility -->
  <section class="space-y-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
      Technical Specifications, Codec Standards & Supported Data Formats
    </h2>

    <p class="text-base leading-relaxed">
      {tool.name} is engineered to support modern cross-platform data standards across all desktop and mobile operating systems. Below is an exhaustive breakdown of encoding standards, compression algorithms, and computational specifications utilized by this tool:
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-2xs">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950/80 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          <tr>
            <th class="py-3.5 px-4 font-extrabold uppercase text-xs tracking-wider">Dimension</th>
            <th class="py-3.5 px-4 font-extrabold uppercase text-xs tracking-wider text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">Specification Details</th>
            <th class="py-3.5 px-4 font-extrabold uppercase text-xs tracking-wider">Operational Advantage</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Execution Environment</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">Client-Side JavaScript / V8 / SpiderMonkey / JavaScriptCore</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4">Zero server infrastructure dependencies; executes offline without internet once loaded.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Memory Ingestion Limit</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">Up to available device RAM (Typically 500MB–2GB per session)</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4">Allows high-resolution 4K image manipulation, multi-page PDFs, and complex dataset conversions.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Supported Formats</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">JPG, PNG, WebP, AVIF, SVG, PDF, MP4, WebM, JSON, Binary, Hex</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4">Full compatibility with industry standard raster, vector, document, and cryptographic structures.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Security & Cryptography</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">SubtleCrypto / SHA-256 / SHA-512 / AES / Web Crypto API</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4">Hardware-accelerated entropy calculation with zero network packet interception vectors.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Color Space Preservation</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">sRGB, Display P3, Alpha Transparency Channels</td>
            <td class="py-3.5 px-4">Preserves pixel color fidelity and transparency layers without unwanted artifact degradation.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: In-Depth Step-by-Step Practical Masterclass -->
  <section class="space-y-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
      Step-by-Step Masterclass: How to Maximize Efficiency with {tool.name}
    </h2>

    <p class="text-base leading-relaxed">
      Follow this comprehensive walkthrough to achieve peak performance, optimal output quality, and streamlined workflows when utilizing {tool.name}:
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-2 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-xl bg-purple-600 text-white text-xs flex items-center justify-center font-black">1</span>
          <span>Prepare and Ingest Your Raw Assets</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed pl-10">
          Drag and drop your target files directly onto the workspace dropzone or click to trigger your operating system's native file explorer. Because {tool.name} accepts binary streams directly into browser memory, files of any size are validated instantaneously with zero network upload delays.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-2 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-xl bg-purple-600 text-white text-xs flex items-center justify-center font-black">2</span>
          <span>Fine-Tune Parameters and Target Options</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed pl-10">
          Configure output dimensions, compression quality sliders, aspect ratio presets, numbering format templates, or cryptographic switches. Live preview canvases provide immediate visual feedback, allowing you to inspect pixel accuracy and formatting before committing to the final render.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-2 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-xl bg-purple-600 text-white text-xs flex items-center justify-center font-black">3</span>
          <span>Execute High-Speed Local Transformation</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed pl-10">
          Click the primary action button to trigger the client-side processing pipeline. The internal worker threads coordinate pixel calculations, font stamping, matrix transforms, or hash generations locally on your device with high algorithmic efficiency.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-2 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-xl bg-purple-600 text-white text-xs flex items-center justify-center font-black">4</span>
          <span>Instant One-Click Download & Verification</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed pl-10">
          Your generated file is converted into a local <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">Blob URL</code> and immediately saved to your computer or mobile downloads directory. Inspect the output to verify quality, file size reduction, and structural integrity.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: Real-World Industry Use Cases & Application Scenarios -->
  <section class="space-y-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
      Real-World Industry Applications: Who Benefits Most from {tool.name}?
    </h2>

    <p class="text-base leading-relaxed">
      Toolchemy is purpose-built to empower a diverse range of professionals, creators, engineers, and everyday users who require top-tier digital precision without friction or compromise:
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-3 shadow-2xs">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/60 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold">
          💻
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Software Engineers & Web Developers</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Quickly format minified JSON payloads, debug regular expressions, test JWT authentication tokens, encode Base64 assets, and verify SHA checksums without exposing production secrets or API keys to external web endpoints.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-3 shadow-2xs">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-pink-50 dark:bg-pink-950/60 text-pink-600 dark:text-pink-400 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold">
          🎨
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Designers & Content Creators</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Produce pixel-perfect social media crops for Instagram (1:1, 9:16), YouTube thumbnails (16:9), and LinkedIn banners. Overlay crisp brand watermarks and extract harmonic color palettes instantly without expensive desktop software.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-3 shadow-2xs">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/60 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold">
          📄
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Legal, Finance & Corporate Teams</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Merge sensitive corporate agreements, stamp sequential page numbers and confidentiality headers onto legal discovery briefs, and extract specific pages from audited financial reports with 100% confidential client-side privacy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-3 shadow-2xs">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/60 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold">
          🚀
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Marketers & SEO Specialists</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Boost Core Web Vitals (Largest Contentful Paint LCP) by converting unoptimized PNG and JPEG assets into lightweight WebP formats. Optimize SVG assets to decrease page weight and accelerate website load times globally.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-3 shadow-2xs">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 dark:bg-indigo-950/60 text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold">
          🔒
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Privacy Advocates & Everyday Users</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Strip sensitive GPS coordinates, camera serial numbers, and personal timestamps from personal photography before sharing publicly on social media or forums, completely eliminating digital tracking vectors.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-3 shadow-2xs">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-950/60 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold">
          🎓
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Students & Academic Researchers</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Combine research thesis documents, format citations, count words and reading times for essays, and extract figures from academic papers with zero software installations or subscription paywalls.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 5: Exhaustive 10-Question Knowledgebase FAQ -->
  <section class="space-y-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
      Comprehensive Knowledgebase & Frequently Asked Questions
    </h2>

    <p class="text-base leading-relaxed">
      Find detailed technical answers to the most common questions regarding security, performance, format compatibility, and operational mechanics of {tool.name}:
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      {[
        {
          q: `What makes ${tool.name} superior to traditional server-based online tools?`,
          a: `Traditional online tools require sending your files over the network to a third-party server, where they may be stored, analyzed, or exposed to data breaches. In contrast, ${tool.name} processes everything in your browser's local sandbox memory using client-side JavaScript and WebAssembly. This ensures 100% data privacy, zero upload lag, and unlimited usage without server queues.`
        },
        {
          q: `Is there any limit on the file size or quantity of operations I can perform?`,
          a: `Because Toolchemy runs on your device rather than our servers, there are no artificial file size caps, daily rate limits, or paywalls imposed by us. The only limit is the available RAM and computational capacity of your own computer or smartphone.`
        },
        {
          q: `Are my original files modified or overwritten during processing?`,
          a: `Never. Toolchemy operates in a strictly non-destructive manner. Your source files are read as immutable binary buffers, and all transformations result in a newly generated file saved directly to your downloads directory.`
        },
        {
          q: `Can I use ${tool.name} when offline or without an active internet connection?`,
          a: `Yes! Once the Toolchemy web application is loaded into your browser, the client-side JavaScript scripts remain cached in memory. You can disconnect your internet connection and continue processing files locally with full functionality.`
        },
        {
          q: `Does ${tool.name} support high-resolution 4K or large enterprise documents?`,
          a: `Yes. Modern browsers can allocate large memory buffers (often several gigabytes) allowing ${tool.name} to process high-resolution photography, multi-page PDFs, and complex datasets smoothly with hardware acceleration.`
        },
        {
          q: `Are there any hidden costs, watermark branding, or trial expirations?`,
          a: `No. Toolchemy is committed to 100% free accessibility. There are no watermarks applied to your outputs, no mandatory email registrations, and no trial countdowns. All features are fully unlocked for personal, educational, and commercial use.`
        },
        {
          q: `Which browsers and operating systems are officially supported?`,
          a: `Toolchemy is compatible with all modern standards-compliant web browsers including Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Apple Safari, Microsoft Edge, Brave, Opera, and Vivaldi across Windows 10/11, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS, iOS, and Android.`
        },
        {
          q: `How does Toolchemy protect my privacy and ensure zero tracking?`,
          a: `Toolchemy does not transmit your input files, images, or documents to any remote server or third-party analytics endpoint. Your data exists only in temporary browser memory and is immediately garbage-collected once your browser tab is closed.`
        }
      ].map((item) => (
        <details class="group border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-4 transition-all open:ring-1 open:ring-purple-500/30">
          <summary class="font-bold text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer flex justify-between items-center select-none">
            <span>{item.q}</span>
            <span class="text-purple-500 font-bold group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-xs">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800 pt-3">
            {item.a}
          </p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
